{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline","id":1270923,"title":"[V5] Timeline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-26T14:23:07-08:00","id":1270923,"title":"[V5] Timeline","content":"Putting together a timeline of events for my own game, and I thought I would share what I had. Input would be appreciated, as I know I missed things.<br /> <br /> 2002 - Admiral Poindexter takes control of the Information Awareness Office. He greenlights a number of DARPA initiatives intended to help expose and combat supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> 2003 - Felicity Price of the C.I.A. heads up project FIRSTLIGHT.<br /> <br /> - the Camarilla feeds information about the Sabbat to government agencies, using them to help burn out the Camarilla's rival sect.<br /> <br /> 2004 - the NSA discovers and penetrates SchreckNET<br /> <br /> 2004 - the Eighth Direction in Russia joins what will come to be called the Second Inquisition. Members include the Newburgh Group from England, BOES in Brazil, and the Society of St. Leopold<br /> <br /> 2004 - The Red Question releases the first version of their manifesto<br /> <br /> 2005 - F.B.I. Special Affairs Division is resurrected due to the work of FIRSTLIGHT. Retired members of Project Twilight are brought in out of retirement to advise.<br /> <br /> [2005 - conjecture - the Sabbat begin the slow migration to the middle east that will be known as the Gehenna Crusade. The year was chosen to coincide with Gehenna from the Revised edition and from contextual clues. Sabbat cities slowly empty out over the span of the next decade]<br /> <br /> 2006 - <i>Anarchs Unbound</i> is officially banned by the Camarilla, and dire warnings are issued about sect members mingling with the Red Question<br /> <br /> 2006 - British anti-terror unit SO13 begins the sterilization of London. This will continue for the next seven years.<br /> <br /> - French units begin exterminating vampires in Paris, causing the Camarilla court to flee the domain<br /> <br /> - Camarilla elders begin to feed information about Anarch holdings as well Sabbat in an attempt to deflect attention from their own domains.<br /> <br /> 2007 - The Red Question deal directly with Camarilla Justicars; the next day the 2007 financial collapse begins<br /> <br /> 2007 - Marcus Questor becomes the agent in charge of the Special Affairs Division, and his ties to the IAO aid in securing intelligence of the blank body phenomenon,<br /> <br /> 2008 - a joint SOCOM task force destroys the Tremere Prime Chantry, decapitating the Tremere pyramid and purging Vienna of Kindred<br /> <br /> - Carna begins her flight across the United States, spreading word of what she has learned from <i>The Book of the Grave War</i> to her followers<br /> <br /> - Anarchs take the opportunity to conquer several weak Camarilla domains<br /> <br /> <br /> 2010 - video leaks to vampire websites showing a member of the Red Question poisoning a Tremere rival in 2001. It is the last highly publicized act of the Red Question.<br /> <br /> 2010 - The Conclave of Galloway convenes; it is decided to ban the Anarchs from membership in the Camarilla, remaking the organization into something exclusively for the vampire elite and their chosen brethren.<br /> <br /> 2011 - Meeting of the Camarilla inner council chooses a new slate of Justicars, elevating Lucinde to Ventrue Justicar for Unlife.<br /> <br /> 2012 - Simultaneous conclaves are held in Chicago and Prague. Theo Bell assassinates Hardestadt (and possibly Jan Pieterzoon) at the Prague Conclave. The Brujah formally leave the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> 2013 - Queen Ann is decapitated in London, effectively concluding the sterilization of the city<br /> <br /> - the Camarilla meets with the Banu Haqim and the Setite Ministry on the same night to weigh the merits of admission into the Camarilla. The Ministry meeting ends prematurely when a bomb levels the hotel where the dignitaries are convening. This results in the Banu Haqim being admitted.<br /> <br /> - the Camarilla takes Mexico city<br /> <br /> 2017 - massive slaughter in Berlin stretches the Masquerade to the breaking point. Berlin becomes an Anarch domain after the Prince is destroyed in the street.<br /> <br /> 2018 - *current* as of the publication of V5<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24680,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24680-jrrparker","user":"JRRParker","date":". 11-26-2018, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24680-jrrparker","name":"JRRParker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T15:20:51-08:00","id":1270947,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the summary from V5 timeline.<br /> <br /> The Prague Conclave where Theo Bell kill Hardestadt is set in 2012 in Camarilla book and Corebook V5 in Hardestadt loresheet(I don't have Anarch book)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24765-faerl","name":"Faerl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T17:00:31-08:00","id":1270979,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I've edited that into the timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24680-jrrparker","name":"JRRParker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:51:46-07:00","id":1333102,"title":"","content":"Is the CIA Felicity Price the same as the NSA Felicity Price ?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://vtesone.wordpress.com/2015/12/16/kindred-lore-nsa-trio/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://vtesone.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/nsatrio.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vtesone.wordpress.com/2015/12/16/kindred-lore-nsa-trio/\" target=\"_blank\"> Kindred Lore: NSA Trio </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vtesone.wordpress.com/2015/12/16/kindred-lore-nsa-trio/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://vtesone.wordpress.com/2015/12/16/kindred-lore-nsa-trio/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In the World of Darkness, there are three operatives with the US National Security Agency (NSA), namely Bruce Higgins, Maurice Edwards, and Felicity Price, which seems to have a significant deal of&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:57:29-07:00","id":1333104,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla takes Mexico City?<br /> <br /> Why not eliminate the whole of the Sabbat while you are at it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T09:29:57-07:00","id":1333110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1333104#post1333104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla takes Mexico City?<br /> <br /> Why not eliminate the whole of the Sabbat while you are at it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can visit the Sabbat then they're hardly mysterious and alien aren't they?<br /> <br /> But yes, good fodder for PCs to retake the city.<br /> <br /> I'm annoyed it's not an Anarch domain, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T11:23:33-07:00","id":1333132,"title":"","content":"Thanks for this, really helpful. <br /> <br /> Have any of you integrated retroactive events to Chronicles taking place currently? How did you do it? *Poof* method, as in, it was always like that? It happened but nobody noticed before? Changed the timeline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T18:22:46-07:00","id":1377618,"title":"","content":"Add to that list; 2019-2020 - Starting with Chicago, some Lasombra defectors from the Sabbat find various levels of &quot;welcome&quot; in Camarilla cities.<br /> <br /> I wonder what other big events of the last two years include.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T20:19:41-07:00","id":1377636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1333132#post1333132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for this, really helpful.<br /> <br /> Have any of you integrated retroactive events to Chronicles taking place currently? How did you do it? *Poof* method, as in, it was always like that? It happened but nobody noticed before? Changed the timeline?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I pick and choose what canon events I want to use, so it depends. It's not like you're beholden to use the canon as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T01:50:11-07:00","id":1377688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1333132#post1333132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for this, really helpful.<br /> <br /> Have any of you integrated retroactive events to Chronicles taking place currently? How did you do it? *Poof* method, as in, it was always like that? It happened but nobody noticed before? Changed the timeline?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I have an ongoing game established events in that game always take precedence over cannon sources. This has been the way I have ran since 1st. Lodin can die in Ashes to Ashes then he is back in CBN 1st ed then dead again in 2nd then back in 5th. there are more than just this. After a while you get used to each edition changing cannon so i stick to the only true cannon for my game is what is in my game. when we reset the game and the whole party creates new characters I may change the cannon for my game. It allows us to play over and over again without always knowing exactly the truth behind everything. Ravnos died, or did he, I mean seriously have you read high level Chemistry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T02:39:46-07:00","id":1377694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JRRParker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline#post1270923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2013 - the Camarilla meets with the Banu Haqim and the Setite Ministry on the same night to weigh the merits of admission into the Camarilla. The Ministry meeting ends prematurely when a bomb levels the hotel where the dignitaries are convening. This results in the Banu Haqim being admitted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Source of this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T09:38:46-07:00","id":1377755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Riccardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1377694#post1377694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Source of this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's in the Camarilla and Anarch books.Talks about it on Cam pg. 158 and Anarch pg. 182. IT doesn't explicitly mention the same night that I can find though. But it talks about the same events from two sides (Banu view in Cam, Ministry view in Anarch).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-01-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:40:37-07:00","id":1377866,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a link or a copy paste of V20 Timeline that I could add to this cool V5 Timeline? I'm looking to build up a good timeline for my game.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8757-pram","name":"Pram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:27:56-07:00","id":1377965,"title":"","content":"Here is one I did for the Second inquisition when 5th was first starting you can use if it helps with more events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279114-inquisition-timeline\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279114-inquisition-timeline\"> Inquisition Timeline - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279114-inquisition-timeline\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1279114-inquisition-timeline </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So While we wait for more V5 Goodness I have decided to start compiling some timelines that I will use in my game. First up is the 2I, since they are a primary </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:03:49-07:00","id":1384698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1377755#post1377755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the Camarilla and Anarch books.Talks about it on Cam pg. 158 and Anarch pg. 182. IT doesn't explicitly mention the same night that I can find though. But it talks about the same events from two sides (Banu view in Cam, Ministry view in Anarch).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's before. Fall of London is set in 2012 and about Hafsa says: &quot;The Banu Haqim Hafsa served the Toreador Justicar Madame Guil for many years before the Odense Pact&quot;, implying that already happened.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T08:35:20-07:00","id":1395600,"title":"","content":"Some useful info to add to timeline specific to Chicago:<br /> * 1993, end of Lupine Wars and death of Prince Lodin<br /> * 1993-2008 Primogen rule of Chicago and battle for the throne<br /> * ~2008-2009 Praxis of Joseph Petersen and the Olympic bid for Chicago<br /> * 2009 Prince Jackson claims throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26014-king0ni","name":"king0ni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T09:47:18-07:00","id":1395611,"title":"","content":"I feel like this stuff would've gone over better had we watched it unfold, rather than had it 'just happen' in the time we werent looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T11:58:13-07:00","id":1395636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395611#post1395611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this stuff would've gone over better had we watched it unfold, rather than had it 'just happen' in the time we werent looking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame a decade and a half of no metaplot. Have to fill in the gaps somehow.<br /> <br /> I will say THE FALL OF LONDON was the best idea Modiphius (?) ever had because suddenly something that was just there is now a Transylvania Chronicles-esque chronicle that fills in a lot of gaps.<br /> <br /> Players and STs alike accept things they can be a part of much better if they're just imposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:34:22-07:00","id":1395646,"title":"","content":"They could've waited, and filled the intermittent period with small back'n forth changes. As much as I've reconcilled with much of V5's metaplot, and even though older editions/revised hammered the metaplot forward, Vampire society works best as a slow changing behemoth. The Pacing of V5 is far too fast (But also, the middle east gehenna war just trickled vampires towards it? Did the Sabbat want to lose?) (but also, framing the Arab spring revolts as a super important backdrop for Gehenna seems both tactless and... not at all how vampires work. There's no good reason to make these wars more important than other wars)<br /> <br /> If V5 opened with Vienna Prime's bombing and the downsizing of the Camarilla and that was it, it would've been <i>dope. </i> If they then put out a Sabbat book with &quot;And there's a new pope who's giving us a crusade order, let's pack up and hit the middle east&quot; then that would've been absolute <i>dope</i>. But instead we wake up from our Torpor (and V20 dream) and find all these things have changed without us. It seems more like someone's fanfiction setting is forced on us, where lots of core features have been inverted for shock value. If you look at some of those things individually, they work really well, but when they're all slapped together like they were, it seems very disconnected to most. If you add something new and shocking and add the justifcation for it at the same time, it isn't great storytelling. You need to set things up before the payoff.<br /> <br /> A great plot you don't tell well is a bad story. After some thinking about it: Some of V5's metaplot could potentially be downright <i>genius *</i>, but to get into that you have to really search through... Some stuff that on the surface level is rather absurd. We wouldn't have had such a big community split had the metaplot development been paced out in installments rather than been delivered in one big retroactive infodump.<br /> <br /> (* A few very big things are genius. There are still things that are downright bad. But perhaps if we saw V5 develop rather than getting a metaplot infodump that stuff would've been mitigated by our reactions. Also the rule changes and their setting implications are just terrible)<br /> <br /> <br /> It would have been a good, safe thing had very little happened in the years between the end of revised and the start of V5. V20 played it safe and most jumped on board. If V20 stayed canon and V5 continued onwards... This forum would be a happier place. We'd argue about specific events constructively and get mad about rules... Oh to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-10-2020, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:42:57-07:00","id":1395651,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24680-jrrparker\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24680\" data-vbnamecard=\"24680\">JRRParker</a> this is great! I love stuff like this. Thank you \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:59:45-07:00","id":1395653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395646#post1395646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could've waited, and filled the intermittent period with small back'n forth changes. As much as I've reconcilled with much of V5's metaplot, and even though older editions/revised hammered the metaplot forward, Vampire society works best as a slow changing behemoth. The Pacing of V5 is far too fast (But also, the middle east gehenna war just trickled vampires towards it? Did the Sabbat want to lose?) (but also, framing the Arab spring revolts as a super important backdrop for Gehenna seems both tactless and... not at all how vampires work. There's no good reason to make these wars more important than other wars)<br /> <br /> If V5 opened with Vienna Prime's bombing and the downsizing of the Camarilla and that was it, it would've been <i>dope. </i> If they then put out a Sabbat book with &quot;And there's a new pope who's giving us a crusade order, let's pack up and hit the middle east&quot; then that would've been absolute <i>dope</i>. But instead we wake up from our Torpor (and V20 dream) and find all these things have changed without us. It seems more like someone's fanfiction setting is forced on us, where lots of core features have been inverted for shock value. If you look at some of those things individually, they work really well, but when they're all slapped together like they were, it seems very disconnected to most. If you add something new and shocking and add the justifcation for it at the same time, it isn't great storytelling. You need to set things up before the payoff.<br /> <br /> A great plot you don't tell well is a bad story. After some thinking about it: Some of V5's metaplot could potentially be downright <i>genius *</i>, but to get into that you have to really search through... Some stuff that on the surface level is rather absurd. We wouldn't have had such a big community split had the metaplot development been paced out in installments rather than been delivered in one big retroactive infodump.<br /> <br /> (* A few very big things are genius. There are still things that are downright bad. But perhaps if we saw V5 develop rather than getting a metaplot infodump that stuff would've been mitigated by our reactions. Also the rule changes and their setting implications are just terrible)<br /> <br /> It would have been a good, safe thing had very little happened in the years between the end of revised and the start of V5. V20 played it safe and most jumped on board. If V20 stayed canon and V5 continued onwards... This forum would be a happier place. We'd argue about specific events constructively and get mad about rules... Oh to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a somewhat similar view to you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> but my view is tempered with the fact that I actually feel like we're going to have a lot of what was happening in the past 15 years filled in versus having the metaplot continually churn forward. We received a loose picture of what was going on in the world with V5's sourcebook and now we're slowly having those elements of the setting filled in.<br /> <br /> 1. Chicago by Night gave us a sense of what a &quot;typical&quot; city of the Camarilla feels like under the Second Inquisition and new Anarch/Camarilla war. It's different but not THAT different and thay alleviated a lot of fears at my table.<br /> <br /> 2. The Fall of London managed to give us a sense of how powerful the Second Inquisition was [not as powerful as they seemed], told us what was up with Mithras, and let the players directly influence things.<br /> <br /> 3. Blood Cults helped us figure out how the Hecata is working, the updates to the Giovanni, and several other bloodlines. It also explained how the Ministry was created from the Followers of Set (it was apparently a lot more complicated than a &quot;rebranding&quot;).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if this continues to be how supplements go from now on. I very much would love THE FALL OF VIENNA as a campaign supplement and think it and THE COUNCIL OF PRAGUE would be natural sourcebooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:10:43-07:00","id":1395657,"title":"","content":"Trying to sell more books to explain better something you didn't explain well is not an endearing feature, especially if by not explaining some things well you turned off a large portion of the playerbase who aren't even going to pirate your future books, let alone buy them. It might've been a really good business strategy had you a testing group to check that most people would like the new story, but I think you'd have made more money if you churned out a saga of events that take place when the books are released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:16:07-07:00","id":1395660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395657#post1395657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to sell more books to explain better something you didn't explain well is not an endearing feature, especially if by not explaining some things well you turned off a large portion of the playerbase who aren't even going to pirate your future books, let alone buy them. It might've been a really good business strategy had you a testing group to check that most people would like the new story, but I think you'd have made more money if you churned out a saga of events that take place when the books are released.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, this is the heyday of V:TM anyway. It had a rough start but V5 has sold like gangbusters and they've made excellent use of social media.<br /> <br /> At the end, most people don't care about the minutia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:45:44-07:00","id":1395661,"title":"","content":"Pen'n paper in general is more popular nowadays. It's a little unfair to compare a product today to a product yesterday (Also, V20 had the absolute worst marketing so it's not really a fair comparison) <br /> <br /> I feel V5 could've been a phenomenal worldwide sensation that people who don't play pen'n paper games would've heard of had they not taken so much risk with the story. From a business perspective they took on too many uneccessary risks and got devisive fan reception for it. I feel V20's metaplot-free approach captured the zeitgeist of today a lot better (The product would be more attractive if things were getting worse and possitive change was a long way off, when In V5 they seem to be getting better and there's a good deal of optimism, you gotta tap into that doomer feel) Whilst I also know that V5's approach to espousing political stances is... Naive, to say the least. <br /> <br /> I feel like saying &quot;V5 is successful so it's good&quot; is like saying &quot;That Marvel film was successful so it's good&quot;. Like, it's a marvel film, of course it's going to be successful, even if it's no good. Even if they're twice as mopey and half as cool, V5 still has vampires in it; of course it's going to do well. <br /> <br /> Moving forward into a cool story would've made such a big buzz whilst what they're doing now, with supplements detailing retroactive changes... That's not as effective as it could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:55:08-07:00","id":1395667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395646#post1395646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>They could've waited, and filled the intermittent period with small back'n forth changes.</b> As much as I've reconcilled with much of V5's metaplot, and even though older editions/revised hammered the metaplot forward, Vampire society works best as a slow changing behemoth.<b> The Pacing of V5 is far too fast</b> (But also, the middle east gehenna war just trickled vampires towards it? Did the Sabbat want to lose?) (but also, framing the Arab spring revolts as a super important backdrop for Gehenna seems both tactless and... not at all how vampires work. There's no good reason to make these wars more important than other wars)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious\u2014how is the current pacing of &quot;these events happened over the ~twenty years since the last metaplot update&quot; faster than your proposed pacing of &quot;all these metaplot changes are happening during the ~two years since fifth edition started&quot;?<br /> <br /> Personally, I can buy the world changing significantly over two decades, much more easily than I can buy the world changing significantly over two years. The fall of Vienna, the fall of London, the changed direction of the Sabbat, the Ministry rebranding, the Camarilla changing tactics, the Anarchs gaining ground, and the Hecata coming together over the course of two decades, I can buy. Over the course of two years, I'd say <i>that's</i> way too fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T14:15:45-07:00","id":1395675,"title":"","content":"From my opinion it would have been better if V20 would have with BJD slowly updated the Metaplot to 2011or mayby 2015 so we have 7 to 11 years for a slow more stale metaplot and then we have 5 to 7 years of bang where suddenly everything changes fast. My biggest gripe is that they had blamed the IS on Vienna. The IS whas a decade to early. If they would have wanted IS it would have been better 2016 with the Syrian War. 2006 Al Quaida would have been much more believable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T14:30:26-07:00","id":1395676,"title":"","content":"Two years is enough. Most of the stuff in V5 is pretty dependent on other things happening at near the same. Finding out a decade of stuff happened when you weren't looking is no good. V5 has inverted a lot of the setting, so even if the events within were paced out nicely over a decade, it's still hard to take in and accept when it all comes in one book. Imagine coming out of Torpor and finding out that America has become communist; Even if it's a very well reasoned story, it's still going to shock you. And the thing with V5 is that most of the reasoning has been left out for other suplements to cover. So it seems like nutty alternate history, like fanfiction, especially when your perfectly functional V20 setting has done things so well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T15:18:53-07:00","id":1395680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395661#post1395661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pen'n paper in general is more popular nowadays. It's a little unfair to compare a product today to a product yesterday (Also, V20 had the absolute worst marketing so it's not really a fair comparison)<br /> <br /> I feel V5 could've been a phenomenal worldwide sensation that people who don't play pen'n paper games would've heard of had they not taken so much risk with the story. From a business perspective they took on too many uneccessary risks and got devisive fan reception for it. I feel V20's metaplot-free approach captured the zeitgeist of today a lot better (The product would be more attractive if things were getting worse and possitive change was a long way off, when In V5 they seem to be getting better and there's a good deal of optimism, you gotta tap into that doomer feel)</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I didn't buy a single V20 product until Beckett's Jyhad Diary and then bought all of the V20 products. I missed out on a lot but V:TM without metaplot has nothing to offer me. I already have metaplot free sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> Metaplot is the only reason to update your books, IMHO.<br /> <br /> But yes, the big success of Paradox has been taking advantage of the international community of World of Darkness that far eclipses the former American based one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whilst I also know that V5's approach to espousing political stances is... Naive, to say the least. </div> </div> </div>A more cynical man than me might have argued that the controversy generated was deliberate as it brought them to national attention multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like saying &quot;V5 is successful so it's good&quot; is like saying &quot;That Marvel film was successful so it's good&quot;. Like, it's a marvel film, of course it's going to be successful, even if it's no good. Even if they're twice as mopey and half as cool, V5 still has vampires in it; of course it's going to do well.<br /> <br /> Moving forward into a cool story would've made such a big buzz whilst what they're doing now, with supplements detailing retroactive changes... That's not as effective as it could be. </div> </div> </div>I disagree and almost posted the Luke Skywalker, &quot;Everything you said was wrong&quot; meme but that would be rude. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is me being gentle in my riposte but Paradox Interactive has succeeded beyond the wildest dreams of their group and will continue to do so with the revival of Bloodlines, successful visual novels, board games, and their multimedia campaign. They obviously believe in the metaplot heavy V5 and that's paid huge dividends for it. V20 was amazing and helped revive the license when it had faded into obscurity. It was artistically great. However, comparing V5 and V20 is pointless at this point.<br /> <br /> Most of the writers of V20 have helped contribute to V5 and a lot of the plots of V20's BJD are being brought into V5 one after the other.<br /> <br /> I think both of us are on the verge of edition warring again. In the end, we have what we have whether it was better or worse for the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-10-2020, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T16:19:43-07:00","id":1395687,"title":"","content":"Man, we can't have any threads without 'BUT I DON'T LIKE V5 AND HERE'S WHY BASED ON ON THIS TOPIC!' can we?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T16:26:26-07:00","id":1395688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395680#post1395680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I missed out on a lot but V:TM without metaplot has nothing to offer me. I already have metaplot free sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> Metaplot is the only reason to update your books, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>And its the exact opposite feelings for me. I much prefer my settings to have an initial setup and then allow me to tell whatever stories I want without the expectation of specific external events occurring.<br /> <br /> For example, let\u2019s say I had a long-running campaign set in London. Then you\u2019re told... oh, all the NPCs you\u2019ve been using are dead now; you should really change your campaign to match this event arbitrarily decided by someone else.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s why I find all metaplot (here defined as events written to occur after the time period the default setting describes) to be detrimental because they\u2019re going to muck with what some Storyteller set up for their campaign and the more your game material references metaplot the less useful later material becomes to those with ongoing campaigns (and this isn\u2019t just a WoD thing; I have the same problem with Forgotten Realms and it\u2019s metaplot).<br /> <br /> By contrast, the things I found useful about V20 were;<br /> <br /> A) My Revised-era Core Book was a twenty-year old falling apart from continual use mess that needed to be replaced and these days a tablet is a much more convenient method of referencing and transporting game books... V20 was a proper bookmarked PDF that I can legally own (vs. a crappy scan you could only have via piracy).<br /> <br /> B) I never had all the old VtM books (Mage was my jam and core and Time of Thin Blood had most of the actual rules I needed to reference as a player) and V20 went out of its way consolidate nearly all the material into the core book that had been scattered across half-a-dozen or more books in the Revised era that I wasn\u2019t even aware existed. In short... more bang for your buck in the V20 books vs. previous editions.<br /> <br /> C) While they were relatively conservative with it, they did clean up some of the mechanics in V20 and I\u2019m not ashamed to admit that 90% of my reason for getting BJD was for the V20 Dhampir mechanics so I could finally let my ToTB rest on my bookshelf instead of subjecting it to further use by use.<br /> <br /> D) By leaving aside any metaplot it ensured that the material was useful to any game I wanted to tell... whether I\u2019m employing all, some or none of the existing metaplot.<br /> <br /> In short, it had everything I needed of a new edition; it replaced my ancient falling apart books, consolidated a bunch of the older material in a more portable format and cleaned up a few rules while not trying to force the mechanics and plot direction on my campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T17:03:53-07:00","id":1395692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395688#post1395688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And its the exact opposite feelings for me. I much prefer my settings to have an initial setup and then allow me to tell whatever stories I want without the expectation of specific external events occurring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which you can do, by ignoring the metaplot.<br /> <br /> The thing is that I've been playing since 1993. I have the first, second, and Revised editions. I had them before I got V20.<br /> <br /> Why would I buy a new edition if it's just the same information I had before?<br /> <br /> I buy new editions so they can give me new material.<br /> <br /> New material requires changes to the clans, setting, and characters. If there's no changes, there's no reason to buy.<br /> <br /> YMMV but that's my position.<br /> <br /> V5 inspired me to buy it because I suddenly had a lot of new events to incorporate into my games and shake them up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T17:14:42-07:00","id":1395698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395680#post1395680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I didn't buy a single V20 product until Beckett's Jyhad Diary and then bought all of the V20 products. I missed out on a lot but V:TM without metaplot has nothing to offer me. I already have metaplot free sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> Metaplot is the only reason to update your books, IMHO.<br /> <br /> But yes, the big success of Paradox has been taking advantage of the international community of World of Darkness that far eclipses the former American based one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A more cynical man than me might have argued that the controversy generated was deliberate as it brought them to national attention multiple times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree and almost posted the Luke Skywalker, &amp;quot;Everything you said was wrong&amp;quot; meme but that would be rude. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is me being gentle in my riposte but Paradox Interactive has succeeded beyond the wildest dreams of their group and will continue to do so with the revival of Bloodlines, successful visual novels, board games, and their multimedia campaign. They obviously believe in the metaplot heavy V5 and that's paid huge dividends for it. V20 was amazing and helped revive the license when it had faded into obscurity. It was artistically great. However, comparing V5 and V20 is pointless at this point.<br /> <br /> Most of the writers of V20 have helped contribute to V5 and a lot of the plots of V20's BJD are being brought into V5 one after the other.<br /> <br /> I think both of us are on the verge of edition warring again. In the end, we have what we have whether it was better or worse for the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with your analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T00:36:45-07:00","id":1395782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1270923-v5-timeline?p=1395687#post1395687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, we can't have any threads without 'BUT I DON'T LIKE V5 AND HERE'S WHY BASED ON ON THIS TOPIC!' can we?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Yeah, don't do this. The report button exists for a reason.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T17:42:22-07:00","id":1395937,"title":"","content":"Great thread. This is very useful if you want to set a chronicle into the period between the end of the nineties and right now.<br /> <br /> As for the complaints that V5 moved things forward too quickly... V5 did just adapt the Gehenna metaplot without Gehenna really happening. So Theo Bell killed Hardestadt, the Endless Night failed and Augustus Giovanni was removed from power, the Tremere prime chantry was destroyed (less so in V5 than in Gehenna obviously), and so on. Stuff like the many Sabbat's vampires growing dissatisfaction with the role of a Sect who preached bout bringing the fight to the Antediluvians but did nothing of the sort was present even in revisited and became one of the seeds of the Gehenna crusade. In the same vein the Beckoning is a stand in for the Withering that happened during Gehenna.<br /> <br /> In truth V5 mostly evolved what was already present in the metaplot of previous editions and incorporated the events from the End Times books (in case of Gehenna both the module and the novel) into the timeline without having all vampires wiped out. So no, V5 metaplot did not move too fast at all. On the other hand I question the execution of some of those developments, expecially the Beckoning, but generally speaking V5 Core (less so the other books, fortunately) tends to make the most recent events in the VtM metaplot to appear rushed, things that had to happen to enforce the return of the game to its perceived origins. Beckoning aside, I like most of V5 metaplot developements but I really think they could use an in depth explanation so players and Storytellers could have an easier time incorporating them into their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T18:14:29-07:00","id":1395942,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> I agree. I really like almost all of the V5 meta","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T18:21:14-07:00","id":1395943,"title":"","content":"Metaplot and I\u2019m happy with the direction the game is going. And if you don\u2019t like certain elements of the metaplot, you\u2019re free to ignore them. The metaplot is (I think) basically just a suggested framework that you and your players are free to modify as you see fit. Fall of London for example has a default outcome, but there are lots of other possible results depending on what your group does during the campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T18:35:25-07:00","id":1395946,"title":"","content":"I feel like the biggest fault of the V5 corebook was:<br /> <br /> * Too many examples of Predator types<br /> * Too much in-universe fiction.<br /> * Too much art<br /> <br /> vs.<br /> <br /> * A write up for all 13 Clans<br /> * A wrie up for the Sabbat<br /> * An explanation of the timeline from 2004.","signature":"<hr cl